WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.735
-♪ Best Friends Challenge ♪

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:05.404
♪ Ooh, yeah ♪

00:00:05.404 --> 00:00:06.773
-It works like
"The Newlywed Game,"

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:08.407
okay, but for friends.
I'm going to read you questions

00:00:08.407 --> 00:00:10.443
about each other from
the best friends box,

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:13.846
and you will write down --
you will write down --

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:15.381
try to write the same answers.

00:00:15.381 --> 00:00:20.820
-By the way, I will put the
apostrophe right there.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.621
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.621 --> 00:00:24.623
-Wow.
-Oh, my God.

00:00:24.623 --> 00:00:25.725
-Here's --

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:26.993
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:30.863
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:30.863 --> 00:00:32.365
-Someone finished high school.

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:34.033
-Here's the --

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:36.703
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.104
-Okay, I got my answer.

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:41.674
No, I didn't ask a question yet.
Here is the first question.

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:46.746
Okay. "If Martin won
the lottery, what would he buy?"

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:48.948
Martin Short, if he won the
lottery, what would he buy?

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:52.218
Steve, you're writing what
you think Marty would answer.

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:55.788
If Martin won the lottery,
what would he buy?

00:00:55.788 --> 00:00:57.623
-Uh-oh.
You have to understand...

00:00:57.623 --> 00:00:58.957
-Clearly, you
have different answers.

00:00:58.957 --> 00:01:02.729
-...my handwriting --
my handwriting is not so good.

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:04.063
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:05.831
I'm now trying to realize --
remember what I wrote.

00:01:05.831 --> 00:01:07.299
-You're writing a book.
-No, you know what?

00:01:07.299 --> 00:01:08.734
I was just doing
a sketch of you.

00:01:08.734 --> 00:01:10.436
What was the question?

00:01:10.436 --> 00:01:13.105
-If Martin won the lottery -- if
Martin won the lottery --

00:01:13.105 --> 00:01:14.774
-Okay, I'll go first.
-Okay, Steve, you go first.

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:16.676
-Friends!
-No, hey no.

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:19.045
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:20.046
-Friends?

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:21.914
[ Applause ]

00:01:21.914 --> 00:01:23.983
-Wait, wait, wait.
Let me put the apostrophe.

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.651
Oh no, there's not.

00:01:25.651 --> 00:01:27.787
-I just would put that period.
-There's no -- yeah, exactly.

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:30.223
That period there, perfect.
-And what is the question again?

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:32.825
-"If Martin won the lottery,
what would he buy?"

00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:36.429
-Another face-lift, but
this time with a real doctor.

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:39.466
[ Laughter ]
[ Band plays ]

00:01:39.466 --> 00:01:40.533
-Already.

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:42.168
[ Applause ]

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:45.938
All right.
This is the next question here.

00:01:45.938 --> 00:01:47.240
-Oh, mama!
-Are you ready for this?

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.341
Guys?

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:50.242
-What happened?
-It came alive!

00:01:50.242 --> 00:01:51.644
-All right, really.

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:53.646
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.715
-Okay.
-"If Steve -- if Steve could be

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:58.084
any liquid,
what liquid would he be?

00:01:58.084 --> 00:01:59.218
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.218 --> 00:02:00.786
-What liquid?

00:02:00.786 --> 00:02:02.155
-Yes.
-That's a --

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:05.391
Who comes up with that?
-It's a deep -- deep question.

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:08.094
If Steve could be any liquid,
what liquid --

00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:09.929
-I hope we write the same thing.
-Yeah.

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:10.997
Hey, no!

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:12.331
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.331 --> 00:02:14.433
-Yeah, I'm not sure if
you're best friends right now.

00:02:14.433 --> 00:02:15.868
If Steve --
-This is going to prove whether

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:18.371
we are or not, huh, Jimmy?
-Yeah, that's right.

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:21.841
-You don't have the "Chicago
Manual of Style," do you?

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.910
Go ahead.
-I didn't bring it with me, no.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.744
It's on my iPhone.

00:02:25.744 --> 00:02:28.348
"If Steve could be any liquid,
what liquid would he be?"

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:29.782
Martin, what did you write?

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:33.886
-I wrote skim milk, because he
looks like a glass of skim milk.

00:02:33.886 --> 00:02:36.689
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:38.157
[ Foghorn ]

00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:39.925
-Oh, my God.

00:02:39.925 --> 00:02:41.427
Oh, God.
You offended Steve!

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:43.496
-Yeah.
I wrote --

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:45.965
I realize this is
just actually bad,

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:49.235
but why would
I want to be a liquid?

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:50.402
-No, that's very interesting.

00:02:50.402 --> 00:02:51.904
That's a very
Steve Martin answer.

00:02:51.904 --> 00:02:53.605
-I'm on another --
I'm on another plane.

00:02:53.605 --> 00:02:55.074
-Yeah, I get it, man.

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:57.176
I get it.
-A dramatic plane.

00:02:57.176 --> 00:02:58.311
-Yeah.

00:02:58.311 --> 00:03:00.045
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.045 --> 00:03:02.648
-Oh, my goodness.
All right, ready for this?

00:03:02.648 --> 00:03:04.884
Marty, "What is the most
embarrassing thing Steve

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:07.153
has ever done?"
-Oh, I know what that is.

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:10.189
-Oh. I know this.

00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:11.691
-You both seem to know this one.

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:15.461
"What is the most embarrassing
thing Steve has ever done?"

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:17.262
It's the Best Friends Challenge,
if you're just tuning in

00:03:17.262 --> 00:03:18.597
right now.

00:03:18.597 --> 00:03:20.266
Martin short and Steve Martin
are seeing if they are

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:21.334
best friends.

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:23.202
-Wow.

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:24.203
-I'm getting a writer's cramp.

00:03:24.203 --> 00:03:25.271
-I'm asking them
a serious question.

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:26.706
-Mine is too lengthy.
-I'm asking them

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:28.073
a serious question.
-Do you have another pad?

00:03:28.073 --> 00:03:30.609
I've run out of paper.

00:03:30.609 --> 00:03:31.777
The Sharpie
never runs out of ink.

00:03:31.777 --> 00:03:33.313
Okay, here we go.

00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:37.016
"What is the most embarrassing
thing that Steve has ever done?"

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:38.517
Uh --
-Whoops.

00:03:38.517 --> 00:03:40.486
-All right.
-Okay.

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:42.421
-Steve, almost there?
-Okay, who goes first?

00:03:42.421 --> 00:03:43.856
All right, Martin goes first.

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:46.391
"What is the most embarrassing
thing that Steve has ever done?"

00:03:46.391 --> 00:03:49.028
-It was a bad moment.

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:52.398
He slapped Barry Manilow because
he thought Barry was me.

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:55.301
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:58.004
-Did he really?
-♪ Oh, Mandy ♪

00:03:58.004 --> 00:04:00.139
-For real, you did that?
-Yes.

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:04.010
-Well --
-In the world of "Late Night."

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:06.746
-Mine is --
-You have to show it to them.

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:08.281
-I'm going to.

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:09.615
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.615 --> 00:04:10.849
-Don't slap him again!

00:04:10.849 --> 00:04:13.585
-Have you ever heard of
a thing called timing?

00:04:13.585 --> 00:04:15.521
-I'm trying to give you some.
-Oh, okay.

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:18.690
-Got confused in a men's room
and dried my hands

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:19.958
on the man next to me.

00:04:19.958 --> 00:04:21.694
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:24.263
[ Foghorn ]

00:04:24.263 --> 00:04:26.532
That's perfect.

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:28.434
That was perfect music.
-That was embarrassing.

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:31.771
-All right.
-Let's do one more here.

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:32.838
-Go to hell!

00:04:32.838 --> 00:04:34.373
-Let's go.

00:04:34.373 --> 00:04:38.311
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.311 --> 00:04:41.814
Let's do one more here.
Complete this sentence.

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:47.253
"Steve has the
world's greatest blank."

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:49.922
Complete this sentence.

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:56.062
"Steve has the
world's greatest blank."

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:57.430
If you're just tuning in,
this is the --

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:59.097
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:59.097 --> 00:05:00.533
All right, here we go.

00:05:00.533 --> 00:05:02.368
Complete the sentence, "Steve
has the world's greatest blank."

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:04.203
Marty, you wrote?

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:06.806
-The greatest collection
of Nazi memorabilia.

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:09.375
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:11.510
-What's wrong with you, man?

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:14.180
What is wrong with you?
That is absolutely not true.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.382
-All right.
I wrote...

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:18.617
Collection of Nazi memorabilia.
-Oh, my God!

00:05:18.617 --> 00:05:20.820
We are best friends!
We are best friends!

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:22.922
-Steve Martin, Martin Short.

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:26.059
Check out their
